NOTE: This log was captured using the original (pre-cleanup) testbench,
where $display in write_data/read_data tasks executes one clock edge
BEFORE the write/read actually completes. That is why every printed
data_out value lags the true FIFO content by one read call (e.g. the
very first read prints "x" instead of "1", the second prints "1" instead
of "10", etc.) This is a display-ordering artifact only -- the waveform
(data_out[31:0] in waveform.png) confirms the FIFO itself pushes and pops
the correct values in the correct order, and full/empty flags toggle
correctly. The updated testbench in tb/synchronous_fifo_tb.sv in this
repo fixes the display ordering so printed values match actual FIFO
output directly.
